Learning to swim is very doable at any age 🏊‍♂️
Here’s a safe, step-by-step beginner plan.

1. Start Where You Feel Safe

Use a shallow pool where you can stand

Have a lifeguard or instructor nearby

Never learn alone in deep water

2. Get Comfortable With Water (Most Important)

Before swimming, you must relax.

Practice:

Walk in the water

Splash water on your face

Submerge your face for 3–5 seconds

Blow bubbles underwater (through mouth and nose)

👉 If you panic, stop and stand up.

3. Learn to Float

Floating = survival skill.

Back float

Hold the pool edge

Lean back, ears in water

Spread arms and legs

Look up, breathe slowly

Front float

Hold the wall

Face in water

Push off gently

Stand up after 2–3 seconds

Practice until floating feels easy.

4. Learn Kicking

Hold the wall or a kickboard.

Legs straight, relaxed

Kick from the hips, not knees

Small, fast kicks

Toes pointed

Practice on your back and stomach.

5. Add Arm Movements (Beginner Stroke: Freestyle)

One arm pulls water back

Other arm recovers above water

Keep face down

Turn head to side to breathe

Don’t rush — coordination comes later.
